35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The apron outside the hall was patched three times. That is not a design flaw; it is a commissioning failure.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, the firms confirm the clay is the real enemy. They will only quote shallow work.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,"@Misaki, that matches my ledger. Planted ground costs triple to keep. The fund won’t cover the paths.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Mio, the roll is down to seven. The volunteers are already stretched thin on weekends.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the counts show people want hard ground. The drainage data confirms the soft ground fails.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"So we have a choice: expensive, fragile greenery, or cheap, durable stone. The data is clear.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"The contractors say deep foundations are a no-go. We must design for shallow, small-plant work.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"The fund terms are a trap. If we spend it on trees, we have no money for the paths.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,The volunteers can’t mow a new meadow. They can sweep a paved plaza. That is the only realistic option.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minako,,The heat readings show the paved areas are the only ones people actually use. The rest is just mud.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I am leaning toward the plan that minimizes the surface area requiring active maintenance.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. The plan with the shallow, hard-surface core is the only one the firms can deliver.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,I support the plan that keeps the planted area small enough to fit the fund’s strict terms.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"I support the plan that relies on the existing volunteer groups for simple, low-skill tasks.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minako,,I support the plan that respects the drainage data and the actual foot traffic patterns.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we are converging on the same conclusion. The data does not lie.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Misaki,,The construction risk is too high for anything else. We must be realistic.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,The financial risk is too high for anything else. We must be sustainable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Asuka,,The staffing risk is too high for anything else. We must be manageable.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minako,,The environmental risk is too high for anything else. We must be practical.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
